>>>

<<<
diagnosis. Pl. -oses (-ōsēz).
===
**diagnosis.** Pl. *-oses* (-ōsēz).
>>>

<<<
diagram makes diagrammatic; see -M-, -MM-.
===
**diagram** makes *diagrammatic*; see ^^-M-, -MM-^^.
>>>

<<<
dialect. For d., patois, vernacular, &c., see JARGON.
===
**dialect.** For *d.*, *patois*, *vernacular*, &c., see ^^JARGON^^.
>>>

<<<
dialectal, -ic, -ical. The natural adjective for dialect would be -ic or -ical, & both forms were formerly used as such, besides serving as adjectives to the noun dialectic; but to avoid confusion dialectal has recently
===
**dialectal, -ic, -ical.** The natural adjective for *dialect* would be *-ic* or *-ical*, & both forms were formerly used as such, besides serving as adjectives to the noun *dialectic*; but to avoid confusion *dialectal* has recently
>>>

<<<
been formed & found acceptance, so that we now speak of dialectic(al) skill, but dialectal words or forms.
===
been formed & found acceptance, so that we now speak of *dialectic(al) skill*, but *dialectal words* or *forms.*
>>>

<<<
dialogist. See GREEK a.
===
**dialogist.** See ^^GREEK G^^.
>>>

<<<
dialogue is neither necessarily, nor necessarily not, the talk of two persons; see TECHNICAL TERMS; for the want of a word confined to two, see DUOLOGUE.
===
**dialogue** is neither necessarily, nor necessarily not, the talk of two persons; see ^^TECHNICAL TERMS^^; for the want of a word confined to two, see ^^DUOLOGUE^^.
>>>

<<<
diapason. Pronounce diapa’zn.
===
**diapason.** Pronounce dī*a*pā'zn.
>>>

<<<
diarchy, dy-. Spell di-. D. is to monarchy as dibasic, dicotyledon, digraph, dimeter, dioecious, dioxide,
===
**diarchy, dy-.** Spell *di-*. *D.* is to *monarchy* as *dibasic, dicotyledon, digraph, dimeter, dioecious, dioxide,*
>>>

<<<
distich, & disyllable, are to monocotyledon, monoxide, monosyllable, & the other mono- words.
===
*distich,* & *disyllable,* are to *monocotyledon, monoxide, monosyllable,* & the other *mono-* words.
>>>

<<<
Monologue & dialogue are not a relevant pair, dialogue having nothing to do with Gk di- two-.
===
*Monologue* & *dialogue* are not a relevant pair, *dialogue* having nothing to do with Gk *di-* two-.
>>>

<<<
diarrhoea, -cea. See =, a.
